Biotechnology engineering combines life sciences, engineering principles, and technology to develop products and processes for healthcare, agriculture, industry, and the environment. It involves modifying living cells or biological systems through methods like genetic engineering and bioprocessing.

Core Areas and Subjects

• Foundational sciences: Cell and molecular biology, biochemistry, microbiology, genetics, and structural biology.
• Engineering & computation: Bioprocess engineering, bioanalytical techniques, bioinformatics, computational biology, and data analysis.
• Applied focus: Genetic editing (such as CRISPR), biopharmaceuticals, vaccines, genetically modified crops, biofuels, and bioremediation.
